"#D8DCEB"},"groups":[{"label":"Creation","color":"#7FB77E"},{"label":"Noah","color":"#4EA8DE"},{"label":"Abraham","color":"#D9A441"},{"label":"Moses","color":"#C05746"},{"label":"David","color":"#B07CD4"},{"label":"New covenant","color":"#E4DFCE"},{"label":"Unassigned","color":"#5A6178"}],"relkinds":[{"key":"quoted-in","label":"Quoted in","color":"#E8C15A","strong":true},{"key":"fulfilled-in","label":"Fulfilled in","color":"#D9715C","strong":true},{"key":"parallels","label":"Parallels","color":"#6E9BD1","strong":false},{"key":"illustrates-doctrine","label":"Illustrates doctrine","color":"#9B8AD1","strong":false},{"key":"part-of-covenant","label":"Part of covenant","color":"#5FBFA0","strong":false}],"counts":{"topics":5,"portals":1,"edges":5,"relations":0,"outbound":0},"nodes":[{"id":"bt_book_rut","p":0,"x":56,"y":109,"s":-1,"g":4,"bk":"RUT","ty":"BOOK_OVERVIEW","t":"Ruth: overview","d":"Ruth, set in the days when the judges ruled, follows Naomi and her Moabite daughter-in-law Ruth from loss in Moab to marriage with Boaz in Bethlehem and the birth of Obed, the grandfather of David.","q":"Can {{name}} summarise the book of Ruth from Moab to the birth of Obed?","ev":["Say where the story is set and when","Say how the book ends with David's line (4:17-22)"],"pp":[[7,1,1,22],[7,2,1,23],[7,3,1,18],[7,4,1,22]],"tier":"contextual"},{"id":"bt_rut_moab_return","p":0,"x":56,"y":239,"s":0,"g":4,"bk":"RUT","ty":"STORY","t":"Naomi and Ruth return from Moab","d":"A famine drives Elimelech's family to Moab, where he and his sons die; Naomi returns to Bethlehem, and Ruth refuses to leave her, pledging that Naomi's people and God will be hers.","q":"Can {{name}} tell what Ruth said to Naomi and why Naomi returned to Bethlehem?","ev":["Retell why Naomi's family went to Moab and what happened to them","Say what Ruth promised Naomi (1:16-17)","Say what Naomi asked to be called and why (1:20-21)"],"pp":[[7,1,1,22]],"tier":"contextual"},{"id":"bt_rut_gleaning","p":0,"x":56,"y":369,"s":1,"g":4,"bk":"RUT","ty":"STORY","t":"Ruth gleans in Boaz's field","d":"Ruth gleans barley and lands in the field of Boaz, a kinsman of Elimelech, who shows her kindness and protection and tells her to stay with his young women; Naomi calls him one of their near kinsmen.","q":"Can {{name}} tell how Boaz showed kindness to Ruth?","ev":["Say how Boaz treated Ruth (2:8-16)","Say what Boaz said about the LORD's reward for Ruth (2:12)","Say what Naomi said about Boaz (2:20)"],"pp":[[7,2,1,23]],"tier":"contextual"},{"id":"bt_rut_threshing_floor","p":0,"x":244,"y":369,"s":1,"g":4,"bk":"RUT","ty":"STORY","t":"Ruth at the threshing floor","d":"At Naomi's direction Ruth goes to Boaz at the threshing floor and asks him as a near kinsman to spread his skirt over her; he praises her character, says there is a nearer kinsman, and promises to act.","q":"Can {{name}} explain what Ruth asked of Boaz and how he answered?","ev":["Say what Naomi told Ruth to do","Say what Boaz said about the nearer kinsman (3:12-13)"],"pp":[[7,3,1,18]],"tier":"contextual"},{"id":"bt_rut_redemption","p":0,"x":432,"y":369,"s":1,"g":4,"bk":"RUT","ty":"STORY","t":"Boaz redeems and marries Ruth","d":"At the gate Boaz offers the nearer kinsman the right to redeem Elimelech's land and take Ruth; he declines, Boaz buys it and takes Ruth as his wife, and their son Obed is born, in the line leading to David.","q":"Can {{name}} explain how Boaz redeemed Ruth and how the book links her to David?","ev":["Describe what happened at the gate","Say what the people and women said (4:11-15)","Trace the line from Pharez to David (4:18-22)"],"pp":[[7,4,1,22]],"tier":"central"},{"id":"bt_book_jdg","p":1,"x":244,"y":499,"s":-2,"g":3,"bk":"JDG","ty":"BOOK_OVERVIEW","t":"Judges: overview","d":"Judges tells of Israel after Joshua's death, repeatedly falling into idolatry, being oppressed, crying out and being delivered by judges, and ends with the refrain that there was no king in Israel and everyone did what was right in his own eyes.","q":"Can {{name}} describe the cycle of sin, oppression, crying out and deliverance in Judges?","ev":["Describe the repeating pattern in Judges 2:11-19","Name several judges and the enemies they faced","Say what 21:25 says about Israel at the end"],"pp":[[6,1,1,36],[6,2,1,23],[6,3,1,31],[6,4,1,24],[6,5,1,31],[6,6,1,40],[6,7,1,25],[6,8,1,35],[6,9,1,57],[6,10,1,18],[6,11,1,40],[6,12,1,15],[6,13,1,25],[6,14,1,20],[6,15,1,20],[6,16,1,31],[6,17,1,13],[6,18,1,31],[6,19,1,30],[6,20,1,48],[6,21,1,25]],"tier":"contextual"}],"edges":[[0,5,0],[1,0,0],[2,1,1],[3,2,1],[4,3,1]],"rel":[]}
